    "needs_teacher_verification": true,
    "note": "Chapter 3 is sourced from the Sri Chaitanya Junior Fastrack chemistry section (book pp.56-61), which prints the question, its star rank and a model answer. Only ONE source book is held for chemistry — the TSBIE Basic Learning Material in hand covers physics only — so the two-book union check is PENDING a second chemistry source. The 1+2+1+1+2+1 mark split is a CLAIM until a Telangana IPE teacher confirms it; the question itself is sourced, not invented. AXIS NOTE: the book labels the internuclear axis x, so the σ bonding MO from 2p is written σ2px; NCERT labels the axis z and writes σ2pz. The card follows the book's axis. The book's energy orderings (π2p below σ2p for N₂; σ2p below π2p for O₂), bond orders (N₂ = 3, O₂ = 2) and magnetic natures (N₂ diamagnetic, O₂ paramagnetic) are all CORRECT and are kept. The figures show the 2s and 2p levels; the σ1s and σ*1s levels are completely filled, cancel each other, and are written in the configuration lines instead of drawn."
