        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "N₂ config",
        "lines": [
          "N (Z = 7): 1s² 2s² 2px¹ 2py¹ 2pz¹",
          "N₂ has 14 electrons. In N₂ the π2p levels",
          "lie BELOW σ2px. The configuration is:",
          {
            "text": "σ1s² σ*1s² σ2s² σ*2s² π2py² π2pz² σ2px²",
            "style": "eq"
          }
        ],
        "why": "The filling order is the whole content of the diagram, so it is written first as one line. For N₂ (and lighter molecules) the π2p pair fills before σ2px — this reversed order is what the examiner checks.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Using the O₂ order (σ2px before π2p) for N₂. For N₂ the π2p levels come FIRST.",
          "Losing count of electrons. The superscripts must add to 14."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Fourteen electrons or fewer: π before σ in the 2p block.",
        "margin_note": "Add the superscripts aloud — 2+2+2+2+2+2+2 = 14 — before moving on."
