        "why": "The diagram mark is for the level ORDER in the middle column: for N₂ the two π2p levels sit below σ2px, all bonding levels are full up to σ2px, and both π* levels are empty. Every electron is paired.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Drawing σ2px below the π2p pair. That is the O₂ order; for N₂ the π levels are lower.",
